      "id": "tech-https://fakeipedia.org",
      "title": "Show HN: Fakeipedia – Wikipedia for worlds that don't exist",
      "description": "Hi HN!Fakeipedia is an automatic world-building platform which takes an imagined world and makes a whole wiki that you can endlessly explore by clicking red links.I came up with this idea a few months ago after playing around with worldbuilding in Gemini, but I didn't want to release it until a powerful enough model could do it justice, and I decided that Argon is creative enough to write articles that are worth reading. I was surprised how well it turned out and how engaging some of the writing actually is.If you want to generate an article there is a nominal charge attached ($0.90), which helps cover AI/Stripe costs, and I think I just about break even. You can also steer the generation ala choose-your-own-adventure books when generating a new article. Everything generated is free and public for everyone to see.I hope you like it and I'm very much open to hearing about new world ideas/features that would make this project better.\n\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50126334\nPoints: 13\n# Comments: 4",
